   296	3. Results
   297	This section summarizes the results of the study.
   298	3.1. Search results
   299	Table A1 (inAppendix 1 ) shows the results of the search proce-
   300	dure. Although we identiﬁed 19 articles by this search process, one
   301	of the articles [19] is a short version of another article [18]. Thus
   302	we identiﬁed 18 unique studies. In addition, we found another
   303	two other studies that had been subject to peer review: one by ask-
   304	ing researchers about their current work [1]and the other by
   305	searching the Simula Research Laboratory website [14]. Other
   306	potentially relevant studies that were excluded as a result of apply-
   307	ing the detailed inclusion and exclusion criteria are listed in Table
   308	A2inAppendix 1 . One of the excluded papers positioned itself as
   309	an EBSE paper but did not specify how it applied the EBSE princi-
   310	ples [26].
   311	Two studies were published in conference proceedings as well
   312	as in journals: Galin and Avrahami [7]is a conference version ofGalin and Avrahami [8]and Kitchenham et al. [20] is a conference
   313	version of Kitchenham et al. [21].
   314	The data extracted from each study are shown in Tables A2 and
   315	A3(inAppendix 1 ). Summaries of the studies can be found in [24],
   316	Appendix 3.
   317	3.2. Quality evaluation of SLRs
   318	We assessed the studies for quality using the DARE criteria (see
   319	Section 2.4). The score for each study is shown in Table 3 . The ﬁelds
   320	marked with an asterisk in Table 3 were originally marked as un-
   321	known and were re-assigned after communicating with the study
   322	authors.
   323	The last column in Table 5 shows the number of questions
   324	where the researchers were in agreement. All disagreements were
   325	discussed and resolved.
   326	The results of the quality analysis show that all studies scored 1
   327	or more on the DARE scale and only three studies scored less than
   328	2. Two studies scored 4 ( [15 and 21] ) and two studies scored 3.5
   329	([14 and 40] ).
