   521	American authors.
   522	The success of the Simula Research Laboratory in applying the
   523	principles of EBSE and performing high quality SLRs is supported
   524	by the strategy of constructing databases of primary studies re-
   525	lated to speciﬁc topic areas and using those databases to address
   526	speciﬁc research questions. A database of cost estimation papers
   527	from over 70 journals [16] has been the basis of many of the de-
   528	tailed cost estimation studies authored or co-authored by Jørgen-
   529	sen and the database of 103 software experiments [36] has
   530	allowed researchers to assess a number of speciﬁc research trends
   531	in software experimentation.
   532	4.4. What are the limitations of current research?
   533	With respect to whether research topics addressed by SLRs are
   534	somewhat limited (RQ4.1), a relatively large number of studies re-
   535	late to research practice rather than questions concerning speciﬁc
   536	software engineering practices and techniques. This is disappoint-
   537	ing since this type of study beneﬁts researchers rather than practi-
   538	tioners, and evidence-based software engineering is meant to be of
   539	beneﬁt to practitioners. However, three of the research trend stud-
   540	ies addressed the quality of current experimental studies and iden-
   541	tiﬁed areas for improvement, and improved empirical methods
   542	might be expected to beneﬁt practitioners in the longer term. Fur-
   543	thermore, the Jørgensen and Shepperd study [16], although classi-
   544	ﬁed as a research trends study, is also an example of a mapping
   545	study (i.e. a study that aims to identify and categorise the research
   546	in a fairly broad topic area). The availability of high quality map-
   547	ping studies has the potential to radically change the nature of
   548	software engineering research. Mapping studies can highlight
   549	areas where there is a large amount of research that would beneﬁt
   550	from more detailed SLRs and areas where there is little research
   551	that require more theoretical and empirical research. Thus, instead
   552	of every researcher undertaking their own research from scratch, a
   553	broad mapping study provides a common starting point for many
   554	researchers and many research initiatives. On September 17,
   555	2008, the SCOPUS search engine found already 23 citations of this
   556	paper of which only four were self-citations. This suggests that the
   557	research community has already recognised the value of a good
   558	mapping study.
   559	For studies that investigated technology questions, the majority
   560	have been in the cost estimation ﬁeld. Of the conventional software
   561	engineering lifecycle, only testing, with three studies, has been
   562	addressed.
   563	Juristo et al. [18,19] found only 24 studies comparing unit test-
   564	ing techniques. This is extremely surprising given that unit testingis a software activity that is relatively easily studied using experi-
   565	ments since tasks are relatively small and can be treated in isola-
   566	tion. We found this particularly curious in the light of 29
   567	experiments that compared test–retest methods of predicting
   568	remaining defects after inspections [32] which is a far less central
   569	element of software engineering practice than unit testing. Juristo
   570	et al.’s study was based on a search of only the ACM and IEEE elec-
   571	tronic databases, so this may be an example of area where a broad-
   572	er search strategy would be useful.
   573	Looking at the number of primary studies in each SLR (RQ4.2),
